WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.238
Before we build anything, here's the
idea that frames this whole guide.

2
00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:08.512
Book 07 doesn't use one certificate
authority for everything.

3
00:00:08.512 --> 00:00:13.087
It gives each kind of certificate its
own source and its own way of renewing.

4
00:00:13.087 --> 00:00:15.513
Intune looks after device certificates.

5
00:00:15.513 --> 00:00:17.900
PIV cards have their own card system.

6
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.725
Domain controllers keep renewing
themselves the way they always have.

7
00:00:21.725 --> 00:00:26.795
What's left — servers, VPN and RADIUS,
SQL, internal websites, appliances,

8
00:00:26.795 --> 00:00:28.841
and anything public-facing —

9
00:00:28.841 --> 00:00:34.000
has nobody renewing it today except
a person with a calendar reminder.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.100
That's the gap the platform fills.

11
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.759
It becomes the system of record for every

12
00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:41.950
certificate Intune and
PIV don't already manage.
